,title,link,text,language,family
0,Guna people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guna_people,"The Guna (also spelled Kuna or Cuna) are an Indigenous people of Panama and Colombia. Guna people live in three politically autonomous comarcas or autonomous reservations in Panama, and in a few small villages in Colombia.","Kuna, Border",Chibchan
1,Guna language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guna_language,"Guna woman selling Molas The Guna language (formerly Kuna or Cuna), spoken by the Guna people of Panama and Colombia, belongs to the Chibchan language family.","Kuna, Border",Chibchan
2,Border Kuna Phoneme Inventory — IPA Lookup,https://ipalookup.com/languages/border-kuna,"The phoneme inventory below shows every sound that functions as a meaningful unit in Border Kuna — a Chibchan language spoken in South America . With 24 phonemes, it has a relatively small inventory compared to the world's languages. Sounds marked with a dashed border (*) are marginal: they appear only in loanwords or highly specialized contexts and are not part of the core phonological system.","Kuna, Border",Chibchan
3,"Vic West - Kuna Kuna ft. Fathermoh, Savara, Brandy Maina & Thee Exit ...",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H059rrXKX1s,"Vic West - Kuna Kuna ft. Fathermoh, Savara, Brandy Maina & Thee Exit Band (Official Music Video)","Kuna, Border",Chibchan
4,"Kuna alphabet, pronunciation and language - Omniglot",https://www.omniglot.com/writing/kuna.htm,"Kuna (Dulegaya) Kuna is a Chibchan language spoken in southeastern Panama and northwestern Colombia by about 50,000 people. There are two varieties of this language. One is known as Kuna, Cuna, San Blas Kuna or Island Kuna, and the other is known as Border Kuna or Mountain Kuna.","Kuna, Border",Chibchan
